  all-records export names; crt.sh states no data licence. They are CA-published certificates, unmodified.

AOSP ca-certificates
  aosp/ holds the Android Open Source Project's platform/system/ca-certificates files, extracted unmodified. AOSP
  declares no licence text for them: the repository's Android.bp gives `license_kinds: ["legacy_by_exception_only"]`
  with an empty `license_text`, and it carries no LICENSE or NOTICE. They are CA-published certificates.

The certificates themselves are public, published by the CAs that issued them.
